i am janet cruz i am a primary school  teacher in the community of cruces  kakawatepek  is a rural village far from acapulco  about a year ago in march it was all  over the news that a pandemic was  affecting much of the world  authorities decided that we wouldn't  travel to rural communities  to protect ourselves the children and  the parents  a year has passed and we have not  returned to the classrooms  [Music]  learning at home is a program used  throughout the country for children to  take classes at home  according to the school grade but it  didn't work in this community  because they don't have tv sets they  don't have internet either  so we decided to travel to this village  every 15 days  to give children their homework on paper  or use textbooks  it's quite a long journey we cross  rivers the only roads are dead roads  we have seen how kids education has  declined  because we have not been in the  classrooms  help from parents has not been what we  hoped for  because most of them can't read or write  they work the fields all day  and the children stay home with no one  to help them with their homework  you open their books and they are empty  there's nothing on the notebooks  it worries me that parents take them  with them to work in the fields  and they might quit school  [Music]  it's going to be hard to get back on  track but with the help of parents  and teachers here at the school it's  possible  we want to motivate the children to help  them continue with their activities  to do the homework that would be a  return strategy
 

